                  esr,\n+                            \"invalid [{}] resolution in lookup mode to an index in [{}] mode\",\n+                            esr.indexPattern(),\n+                            indexNameWithModes.values().iterator().next()\n+                        )\n+                    );\n+                }\n+\n+            }\n+\n+            // this check is crucial for security: ES|QL would use the concrete indices, so it would bypass the security on the alias","submitted_line":109},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The removal of the lookup mode validation from `resolveIndex` and its addition to `postAnalysisVerification` is a good refactoring. The new method `postAnalysisVerification` in `LookupJoin` ensures that aliases are not allowed for LOOKUP JOIN, which is crucial for security. The validation of index patterns in `postAnalysisVerification` ensures that only concrete indices are used, preventing bypassing of security through aliases. The refactoring of `resolveIndex` and the addition of `postAnalysisVerification` improve maintainability by separating concerns.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-12478:13788-","promptId":"#RCM5Y","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":12478,"endPos":13788,"startLine":240,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":269,"endLineOffset":13,"length":1311}],"dstChanges":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java--2947:4518","promptId":"#65M82","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java"